# MarketHunter Experiment 1 runtime - environment file example.
#
# Entirely optional: EXPERIMENT1_DB_PATH already defaults to
# data/experiment1.db relative to WorkingDirectory= (the same default
# api/experiment1_api.py itself uses), so this file is only needed if
# the real deployment's Experiment1 sqlite db lives somewhere else.
#
# If used, copy this to
# /home/ubuntu/MarketHunter/deploy/systemd/experiment1-runtime.env
# (matching EnvironmentFile=-... in experiment1-runtime.service - the
# leading "-" already makes a missing file harmless, this is not a
# required secret file the way Outcome Intelligence's is).

#EXPERIMENT1_DB_PATH=/home/ubuntu/MarketHunter/data/experiment1.db

# GIL Decision Slack envelope ingest (see docs/experiment1-gil-slack-adapter.md)
# is entirely optional and OFF by default - the runtime cycle skips the
# step whenever EXPERIMENT1_GIL_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN is unset, never
# fabricating a connection. It is NOT the same credential as
# OUTCOME_INTELLIGENCE_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL below - that is a write-only
# incoming webhook URL with no read API at all. A Slack Bot User OAuth
# token (xoxb-...) with the channels:history (or groups:history, for a
# private channel) read scope, invited into #global-investment-lab,
# must be provisioned separately before this can ever be set for real.
#EXPERIMENT1_GIL_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...
# Only needed to override the allowlisted #global-investment-lab
# channel_id (verified as C0BNACTF4E4) - leave unset in production.
#EXPERIMENT1_GIL_SLACK_CHANNEL_ID=C0BNACTF4E4
